From: Artem Bambalov <artembambalov1993@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] c2softhevcdec: write with the stride the buffer actually has

The same defect as 0003 and the same upstream fix, one decoder over.

C2SoftHevcDec hands ihevcd the plane pointers of a mapped gralloc buffer
and names the row pitch separately, as ALIGN128(mWidth), assuming the
allocation came back with rows that far apart. This board's gralloc rounds
the stride to a power of two -- 1920 becomes 2048, measured -- so every
luma row is written short of where it belongs, the picture shears and the
tail of the plane is never written.

Carried unverified: there is no HEVC material on this device to decode in
software, and the hardware decoder takes what there is. What makes it worth
applying anyway is that the AVC version of exactly this change was measured
on this hardware and fixed the picture, the two files differ only in which
library they drive, and the change is upstream's, not ours.

The size check in setDecodeArgs has to move with it. It was written when
displayStride and the width the block was fetched with were the same
number, and reads

    if (outBuffer->width() < displayStride || ...)

-- a width in pixels against a row pitch in bytes. Once the pitch comes
from the buffer, the two part company by exactly the padding, and on this
board the check turns down the very buffer it was handed: 384 wide with a
512 pitch is reported as "Output buffer too small: provided (384x240)
required (512x240)", setDecodeArgs returns false, and the component ends
the work item with C2_CORRUPTED. MediaCodec passes that on as err 0xe and
the frame never arrives, which is what an empty video thumbnail in the
gallery is made of.

A block is big enough when it is at least as wide as the picture, so that
is what it is now compared against. Its pitch is its own business.

---
diff --git a/media/codec2/components/hevc/C2SoftHevcDec.cpp b/media/codec2/components/hevc/C2SoftHevcDec.cpp
--- a/media/codec2/components/hevc/C2SoftHevcDec.cpp
+++ b/media/codec2/components/hevc/C2SoftHevcDec.cpp
@@ -515,10 +515,30 @@
                                   size_t inSize,
                                   uint32_t tsMarker) {
     uint32_t displayStride = mStride;
+    if (outBuffer) {
+        C2PlanarLayout layout;
+        layout = outBuffer->layout();
+        displayStride = layout.planes[C2PlanarLayout::PLANE_Y].rowInc;
+    }
     uint32_t displayHeight = mHeight;
     size_t lumaSize = displayStride * displayHeight;
     size_t chromaSize = lumaSize >> 2;
 
+    /*
+     * Only when the pitch can hold a row of the picture. ihevcd checks
+     * exactly that and turns down anything narrower with
+     * IHEVCD_INVALID_DISP_STRD, and a refused pitch leaves the decoder
+     * writing rows the width it last agreed to while the buffer is laid
+     * out for another -- which arrives as a sheared frame with the tail
+     * of the plane never written, showing through green. A block too
+     * narrow for the picture is caught below and the frame is dropped
+     * rather than decoded into the wrong shape.
+     */
+    if (displayStride >= mWidth && mStride != displayStride) {
+        mStride = displayStride;
+        if (OK != setParams(mStride, IVD_DECODE_FRAME)) return false;
+    }
+
     ps_decode_ip->u4_size = sizeof(ivd_video_decode_ip_t);
     ps_decode_ip->e_cmd = IVD_CMD_VIDEO_DECODE;
     if (inBuffer) {
@@ -534,7 +554,7 @@
     ps_decode_ip->s_out_buffer.u4_min_out_buf_size[1] = chromaSize;
     ps_decode_ip->s_out_buffer.u4_min_out_buf_size[2] = chromaSize;
     if (outBuffer) {
-        if (outBuffer->width() < displayStride || outBuffer->height() < displayHeight) {
+        if (outBuffer->width() < mWidth || outBuffer->height() < displayHeight) {
             ALOGE("Output buffer too small: provided (%dx%d) required (%ux%u)",
                   outBuffer->width(), outBuffer->height(), displayStride, displayHeight);
             return false;
@@ -752,24 +772,21 @@
         ALOGE("not supposed to be here, invalid decoder context");
         return C2_CORRUPTED;
     }
-    if (mStride != ALIGN128(mWidth)) {
-        mStride = ALIGN128(mWidth);
-        if (OK != setParams(mStride, IVD_DECODE_FRAME)) return C2_CORRUPTED;
-    }
     if (mOutBlock &&
-            (mOutBlock->width() != mStride || mOutBlock->height() != mHeight)) {
+            (mOutBlock->width() != ALIGN128(mWidth) || mOutBlock->height() != mHeight)) {
         mOutBlock.reset();
     }
     if (!mOutBlock) {
         uint32_t format = HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_YV12;
         C2MemoryUsage usage = { C2MemoryUsage::CPU_READ, C2MemoryUsage::CPU_WRITE };
-        c2_status_t err = pool->fetchGraphicBlock(mStride, mHeight, format, usage, &mOutBlock);
+        c2_status_t err =
+            pool->fetchGraphicBlock(ALIGN128(mWidth), mHeight, format, usage, &mOutBlock);
         if (err != C2_OK) {
             ALOGE("fetchGraphicBlock for Output failed with status %d", err);
             return err;
         }
         ALOGV("provided (%dx%d) required (%dx%d)",
-              mOutBlock->width(), mOutBlock->height(), mStride, mHeight);
+              mOutBlock->width(), mOutBlock->height(), ALIGN128(mWidth), mHeight);
     }
 
     return C2_OK;
